urname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Erner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Guyet-Rousset</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Revuz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Roujeau</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Minocycline as possible cause of severe and protracted hypersensitivity drug reaction</article-title><source>Arch Dermatol</source><year>1995</year><volume>131</volume><fpage>490</fpage><lpage>491</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7726598</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archderm.131.4.490</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mills</surname><given-names>RM</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Severe hypersensitivity reactions associated with allopurinol</article-title><source>Jama</source><year>1971</year><volume>216</volume><fpage>799</fpage><lpage>802</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4252397</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.216.5.799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacNeil</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Haase</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Tremaine</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Marrie</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fever, lymphadenopathy, eosinophilia, lymphocytosis, hepatitis, and dermatitis: a severe adverse reaction to minocycline</article-title><source>J Am Acad Dermatol</source><year>1997</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>347</fpage><lpage>350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9039216</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>